  "question": {
    "text": "In hydrogen discharge tube, it is observed that through a given cross-section <math><mn>3.13</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>15</mn></mrow></msup></math> electrons are moving from right to left and <math><mn>3.12</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>15</mn></mrow></msup></math> protons are moving from left to right per second. The current in the discharge tube (in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>mA</mi></math>) will be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "1",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Number of electrons <math><msub><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3.13</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>15</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br />Number of protons <math><msub><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3.12</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>15</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br />Now, the current is given by the relation<br /><br /><math><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></math><br /><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mn>3.13</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>15</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1.6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>19</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3.12</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>15</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1.6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>19</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>mA</mi></math><br /><br />Now, due to excess the charge on electrons, the direction of the current will be towards the right.",
